Description: Computes alpha and beta diversity metrics in a parallel,
    memory-efficient manner using 'C' and 'pthreads'. Implements 51 classic,
    compositional, and phylogenetic indices including 'Shannon', 'Bray-Curtis',
    'Faith', 'JSD', 'Hellinger', 'Robust Aitchison', and the 'UniFrac' family.
    Ordinates beta diversity distances by principal coordinates analysis
    (with optional negative-eigenvalue corrections), metric and non-metric
    multidimensional scaling, 'Isomap', 't-SNE' and 'UMAP', and constrains
    them by distance-based redundancy analysis and constrained analysis of
    principal coordinates; ordinates count tables by principal components
    analysis and robust Aitchison PCA; and fits variables onto ordinations.
    Tests distances with PERMANOVA, PERMDISP, ANOSIM, MRPP and Mantel tests.
    Several methods are ported from 'scikit-learn', 'scikit-bio', 'gemelli'
    and 'uwot'.
    Provides random sub-sampling for table rarefaction and parses 'Newick'
    trees into 'phylo' objects. Integrates with data structures from
    'phyloseq', 'rbiom', and other common 'bioinformatics' packages.
    Algorithms are described in Smith 'et al.' (2026) <doi:10.21105/joss.09777>.
